{
  "delta_from_prior": "Upgrades from 20-variable Neon58 (peak 8, disjoint link-twin pairs) and 20-variable Neon119 (peak 9, C8 cycle) to a 24-variable, 306-clause instance compressing via 8 XOR pairs to a 16-variable, 64-clause quotient that breaks link-twin product structure and blocks depth-4 size-nonincreasing DP elimination across all 16 branches of (a1, c1, a2, c2), targeting peak 16 while keeping core_refutation UNKNOWN at both stages and remaining within Lean and runtime budgets.",
  "explanation": "### Code Audit of Pinned v5 (`blq-composed-core-scc-emra-ialh5-v5`)\n\nAuditing the supplied v5 solver, `compression.py`, `core_refutation.py`, and the pinned `check_scc_and_growth.py` / `test_elim.py` / `test_mra.py` dependencies yields **no correctness bug**:\n- **`compression._verify_certificate`** rebuilds exact-support blocks from *every* normalized original clause (`for c in original`), checks `len(counts) == len(blocks)` and `sum(counts) == len(quotient)`, verifies `forms[i] & ~mask == 0` for every quotient coordinate used in each block, checks local truth-table equality on all `points(support)`, and verifies every entry of `P * L = I` over GF(2). Fable61's earlier concern about omitted original clauses is not present in the supplied code.\n- **`core_refutation.probe`** enforces an explicit subset gate (`set(core).issubset(set(f))`), compresses `core` via `compress_root`, and returns `UNSAT` *only* when the verified quotient is 2-SAT and `two_sat(q)` is `False`. Composing `probe` once on an exact-compression quotient preserves soundness by equisatisfiability.\n- **`run_counting_core`** verifies every IALH-5 contradiction with exact `Fraction` arithmetic (`verify_certificate`) over full-input-UP-filtered tables, applies sound `signed_scc` literal merging, size-nonincreasing DP (`elim_plus`), and stronger-disjunct pruning (`prune`, dropping `g` only when `g != h` and `below(g, h)`).\n\nI also acknowledge the receipt falsifying my earlier Neon54/55 K6 near-parity witnesses (actual peak 0 via global IALH-5 congruences) and do not repeat that construction.\n\n### Construction: 24-Variable Augmented Bipartite Pair-Transversal Contradiction\n\nWe target **exact compression + composed-core failure + depth-4 DP blocking** on a larger 24-variable instance (306 clauses, max width 8) that compresses cleanly to a 16-variable, 64-clause quotient:\n\n1. **Quotient variables (16) and 8-XOR-pair lifting (24 original variables):**\n   - Left side (8 quotient vars): singletons `a1=1, a2=3, a3=5, a4=7` and XOR pairs `b1=9^10, b2=13^14, b3=17^18, b4=21^22`.\n   - Right side (8 quotient vars): singletons `c1=2, c2=4, c3=6, c4=8` and XOR pairs `d1=11^12, d2=15^16, d3=19^20, d4=23^24`.\n   - Encoding rule (matching Neon58): positive `+(u^v)` expands to `[u, v]` and `[-u, -v]`; negative `-(u^v)` expands to `[-u, v]` and `[u, -v]`.\n\n2. **Quotient clauses (64 blocks, all width 4) and exact original clause counts (306 clauses):**\n   - **`N_L` (16 blocks, 81 original clauses, max width 8):** all 16 negative clauses `(-u1, -u2, -u3, -u4)` with `u_i in {a_i, b_i}`, forcing at least one base pair `P_i = (a_i, b_i)` to `(0, 0)`.\n   - **`N_R` (16 blocks, 81 original clauses, max width 8):** all 16 negative clauses `(-v1, -v2, -v3, -v4)` with `v_j in {c_j, d_j}`, forcing at least one base pair `Q_j = (c_j, d_j)` to `(0, 0)`.\n   - **`C` (32 blocks, 144 original clauses, max width 7):**\n     - Base 16 blocks (64 clauses, width 6): `(a_i, b_i, c_j, d_j)` for `i, j in {1..4}`. Already UNSAT with `N_L` and `N_R` (independent oracle UNSAT).\n     - Overlapping augmentation (16 blocks, 80 clauses): add `P5=(a1,a2)` and `P6=(b3,b4)` crossed with `Q1..Q4` (8 + 32 clauses), and `P1..P4` crossed with `Q5=(c1,c2)` and `Q6=(d3,d4)` (8 + 32 clauses).\n\n3. **Exact root compression & composed-core behavior (not a skip):**\n   - All 64 blocks have distinct supports and single-orbit forbidden sets (`len(z) = 2^j` for `j <= 4` XOR pairs in the block). Total local space points = `1296 + 1296 + 2304 = 4896 <= 16384`; verification work is well under `8,000,000`.\n   - Block-frequency + Hamming-weight tie-breaking in `compress_root` (`(-count, popcount, mask)`) deterministically selects the 16 basis forms in exact order:\n     - Count 18, weight 1: `a1, c1, a2, c2` -> quotient IDs `1, 2, 3, 4`.\n     - Count 18, weight 2: `b3, d3, b4, d4` -> quotient IDs `5, 6, 7, 8`.\n     - Count 14, weight 1: `a3, c3, a4, c4` -> quotient IDs `9, 10, 11, 12`.\n     - Count 14, weight 2: `b1, d1, b2, d2` -> quotient IDs `13, 14, 15, 16`.\n     - Every non-basis linear combination appears in at most 8 blocks (`< 14`), so greedy basis discovery is exact and compatible, and the compression certificate is eligible for automatic Lean verification.\n   - **`core_refutation.probe` returns `UNKNOWN` (`no_clauses_removed`) at both stages:** every original block is already a complete coset of its stabilizer, and every quotient block has size 1.\n\n4. **Why residual branching grows to predicted peak 16 (vs Neon58 peak 8 and Neon119 peak 9):**\n   - In Neon58, ascending quotient order branches `a1, c1, a2, c2` at depths 1\u20134. Whenever `a1=a2=1`, only 2 Left pairs survive, so untouched Right variables have `len(pos)=2` and `len(neg)=2` (`2*2 = 4 <= 2+2`), triggering `elim_plus` DP elimination and killing 7+ states at depth 4 (capping peak at 8).\n   - Here, adding `P6=(b3,b4)` and `Q6=(d3,d4)` keeps `len(pos) >= 3` for every surviving variable even in the tightest depth-4 branch `(a1=1, c1=1, a2=1, c2=1)` (`3*2 = 6 > 5`), completely blocking `elim_plus` across all 16 branches of `(a1, c1, a2, c2)`.\n   - All 16 depth-4 states are pairwise incomparable under `below` (so `prune` drops none), and no width-<=5 UP window yields a linear/congruence contradiction (so IALH-5 returns `UNKNOWN`), giving a predicted frontier of **16** at depth 4.\n   - At depth 5 (`b3`) and depth 6 (`d3`), `N_L` and `N_R` drop to 2 clauses (`len(neg)=1` on `a4, b4` / `c4, d4`), triggering DP collapse so total search stays compact enough to finish within the 20s candidate budget.\n\n5. **Challenge to Fable73's proposed nonlinear link-twin contraction & SAT control:**\n   - Neon58's quotient factors through disjoint OR-twins `y_i = a_i OR b_i`, `z_j = c_j OR d_j` into 2-SAT. Our overlapping pairs `P5, P6, Q5, Q6` couple variables across distinct base pairs, destroying disjoint link-twin equivalence without adding any linear kernel.\n   - **Nearby SAT control:** removing the single 4-clause block `P1 x Q1` (`[1, 9, 10, 2, 11, 12]` etc.) makes the instance SAT (set `a1=b1=0`, `c1=d1=0`, and all other quotient variables `1`: `N_L`, `N_R`, and every remaining positive clause including `P5, P6, Q5, Q6` are satisfied).\n\nThis is a finite residual-growth and compression-stress fixture on pinned v5, not an asymptotic lower bound; controlling total preprocessing, certificate, and residual work on kernel-free nonlinear families remains open.",
